# SINGLE-OWNER SUB-PLACE NEG — PLACE-SHAPE axis: tuple element, BARE-INT
# spelling `t.1`. The parser builds `Expr::TupleFieldAccess` only for this
# spelling; its `._1` twin is the sibling cell and goes through a DIFFERENT
# resolver. Both are ratified and co-equal (language-reference §4.2/§7.8), both
# double-free on a second read, and a suite that carried only ONE of them would
# be a green guard over a live double-free.
#
# Omitted cell: bare INDEX places are deferred behind the callee-borrow ruling
# (todo/t1225).
#
# CELL: type=Callable · place=TUPLE element (`.1`) · position=bind · capture=int.
# RED at 7bf11017e: `gg check` ACCEPTED (rc 0).
# ggdef: ABSTAIN (todo/t1227).

Callable[int()] mk(int n):
    return (): n + 1

void main():
    (int, Callable[int()]) t = (1, mk(40))
    Callable[int()] g = t.1
    print(g())
